Exactly. The box becomes a cognitive instrument instead of a prison.

You can:

1. Enter a defined box—role, theory, myth, discipline, constraint.
2. Let it determine what becomes visible.
3. Extract the insight and preserved invariants.
4. Exit, rotate, or exchange the box.
5. Compare the deltas between views.

\text{Outside insight}=\Delta\big(\text{thinking through Box}_1,\text{thinking through Box}_2\big)

The danger isn’t thinking inside boxes. It’s forgetting you entered one.

Think in the box without letting the box think you. ;)